                    },
                    "message": "Need afterGetSubProcessorCorePresent  here?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor_core.hpp",
                    "line": 125,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "I think '(ec.value() == EBADR)' implies the interface \"Present\" does not exist.\nIn other cases, it seems ignored, e.g, Fan - https://github.com/openbmc/bmcweb/blob/master/redfish-core/lib/fan.hpp#L249"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor_core.hpp",
                    "line": 136,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Gunnar Mills",
                        "email": "gunnar@gmills.xyz",
                        "username": "gtmills"
                    },
                    "message": "What if you have Present and not available ? They seem independent"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor_core.hpp",
                    "line": 136,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Myung Bae",
                        "email": "myungbae@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "baemyung"
                    },
                    "message": "Both Present and Availability are resulting into [\"State\"][\"State\"] field.\n\nThe current code sets like this (assuming those interfaces exist)\n\nThe current code:\n\n- !present && available \"[State\"] = Absent\n- !present && !available: \"[State\"] = Absent\n- present && available: [\"State\"] = OK\n- present && !available : [\"State\"] = UnavailableOffline\n\n\nShould we remove \"availablity\" from this check like many other cases?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "redfish-core/lib/processor_core.hpp",
                    "line": 136,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Janet Adkins",
                        "email": "janeta@us.ibm.com",
                        "username": "jeaaustx"
                    },
                    "message": "I wonder if it would be clearer the interaction of these D-Bus properties if the available state is sent down to the afterGetSubProcessorCorePresent() function and then the Status/State is set in there based on both of the properties?"
                }
            ],
